Let $frak(g) = frak(g)_0^RR$, where $frak(g)_0$ is a simple Lie algebra over
$CC$. Making use of the normal real form of $frak(g)_0$ we may identify
$frak(g)(CC) tilde.eq frak(g)_0 plus.o overline(frak(g))_0$ with
$frak(g)_0 plus.o frak(g)_0$. A dominant weight of $frak(g)(CC)$ is expressed in
the form $Lambda = (Lambda_1, Lambda^1)$, where $Lambda_1, Lambda^1$ are
dominant weights of $frak(g)_0$. The condition
$rho(Lambda) tilde.op overline(rho(Lambda))$ is expressed by the identity
$Lambda_1 = Lambda^1$ with $epsilon(rho(Lambda)) = 1$.

Finally, let us describe how to calculate the index of a representation of any
semisimple Lie algebra $frak(g)$ over $RR$. Let
$frak(g) = plus.o.big_(1 <= i <= s) frak(g)_i$, where $frak(g)_i$ are simple,
and $Lambda = (Lambda_1, ..., Lambda_s)$, where $Lambda_i$ is a dominant weight
of $frak(g)_i (CC)$. Then $rho(Lambda) tilde.op overline(rho(Lambda))$ if and
only if $rho(Lambda_i) = overline(rho(Lambda_i))$ for all $i = 1, ..., s$ and
$epsilon(rho(Lambda)) = product_(1 <= i <= s) epsilon(rho(Lambda_i))$.
